><article-title>Education, prevalence of disease and frequency of health care utilisation</article-title><source>The 1983 Italian National Health Survey</source></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kasirye</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Ssewanyana</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Nabyonga</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lawson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Demand for health care services in Uganda: implications for poverty reduction</article-title><year>2004</year></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blakely</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ivory</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Commentary: Bonding, bridging, and linking-but still not much going on</article-title><source>Intern J Epidemiology</source><year>2006</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>614</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/ije/dyl084</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kavanagh</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Turrell</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Subramanian</surname><given-names>SV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Does area-based social capital matter for the health of Australians?</article-title><source>A multilevel analysis of self-rated health in Tasmania International Journal of Epidemiology</source><year>2006</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>607</fpage><lpage>13</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kawachi</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Kennedy</surn